            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 6 m5-001: The uninit keyword can only be used as the right-hand side of a mutable let binding (let mut). To fix this, either add the mut keyword to the let binding or provide a proper initialization value. Example: `let mut x: u64 = uninit;` is valid, but `let x: u64 = uninit;` is not."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0220",
              "id": "P0220",
              "name": "uninit only valid for let mut",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "uninit marker not allowed in immutable let binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 6 m5-001: The uninit keyword can only be used as the right-hand side of a mutable let binding. It cannot appear as a general expression in function calls, return statements, or other contexts. Use it only in patterns like `let mut x: Type = uninit;`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0221",
              "id": "P0221",
              "name": "uninit not valid in this position",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "uninit keyword only valid as RHS of let mut binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "PA10-006u: In static initializers (module-level let bindings), & can only be applied directly to a symbol name, not to arbitrary expressions. For example, `let p: u64 = & target;` is valid, but `let p: u64 = & (expr);` is not. Address-of-expression patterns must be used in runtime contexts, not static initialization."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0230",
              "id": "P0230",
              "name": "address-of requires identifier in static initializer",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "& must be applied to a simple symbol identifier"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "PA10-006u: Mutable references (& mut) are not allowed in static initializers (module-level let bindings). Only immutable addresses are supported. Use `let p: u64 = & symbol;` (without mut)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0231",
              "id": "P0231",
              "name": "mutable reference forbidden in static initializer",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "& mut cannot be used in static initializers"
