              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The #![bits = N] inner attribute specifies the target word size. Valid values are 32 or 64. Specifying 16 emits B1700 (16-bit mode not supported). Other values like #![bits = 99] are invalid. Supply one of the three allowed values, or omit the attribute to use the default."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0240",
              "id": "P0240",
              "name": "Invalid #![bits] value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "#![bits] requires 32 or 64 (16-bit mode emits B1700)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 16 m4-001: The #![target_features = \"name\"] attribute specifies a CPU feature token that is not recognized. Valid feature tokens are: cx16, popcnt, bmi1, sse4.2, avx, avx512f. These correspond to x86_64 CPU capabilities that may be assumed for code generation. Other feature names are invalid or not yet supported. Check the feature name spelling against the accepted set, or file an issue to request additional CPU feature support."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0241",
              "id": "P0241",
              "name": "Unknown CPU feature token",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "the CPU feature name is not in the accepted set (cx16, popcnt, bmi1, sse4.2, avx, avx512f)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 10 PA10-006y: A postfix symbol attribute was used on a let declaration, but the attribute name is not recognized. Currently, only '@align(N)' is supported for per-symbol alignment. Check that the attribute name is spelled correctly. Example: `let mut pml4 : [u64; 512] = uninit @align(4096)`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0250",
              "id": "P0250",
              "name": "Unknown symbol attribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "only '@align' is supported as a symbol attribute"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 10 PA10-006y: The @align directive is syntactically malformed. The correct syntax is '@align(N)' where N is an integer literal. Either the opening '(' after 'align' is missing, or the closing ')' after the value is missing. Example: `let mut pml4 : [u64; 512] = uninit @align(4096)`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0251",
              "id": "P0251",
              "name": "Malformed @align directive",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@align(N) syntax error: expected '(' after 'align' or ')' after value"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 10 PA10-006y: The @align directive's value must be a positive integer that is a power of two, and must fit in the range [1, 2^30] (i.e., 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, ..., 1073741824). Common alignment values are 1, 4, 8, 16, 4096, 65536. Check that the value is a valid power of two and not too large."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0252",
              "id": "P0252",
              "name": "Invalid @align value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@align value must be a power of two in range [1, 2^30]"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive is syntactically malformed. The correct syntax is '@ring(slots=N, slot_size=M)' where N and M are integer literals. N must be a power of two > 0, and M must be > 0. Either a required parameter is missing, the format is incorrect, or closing parentheses are missing. Example: `let mut ring_buf : [u64; 512] = uninit @ring(slots=256, slot_size=32)`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0253",
              "id": "P0253",
              "name": "Malformed @ring directive",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring(slots=N, slot_size=M) syntax error"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive's slots parameter must be a positive integer that is a power of two. Valid slots values: 1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, etc. Check that the slots value is a power of two and not zero."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0260",
              "id": "P0260",
              "name": "Invalid @ring slots value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring slots must be a power of two and > 0"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 14 PA14-r14-008: The @ring directive's slot_size parameter must be a positive integer, and the total size (slots * slot_size) must not overflow a 64-bit integer. Check that slot_size is > 0 and not too large."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0261",
              "id": "P0261",
              "name": "Invalid @ring slot_size value or overflow",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@ring slot_size must be > 0 and not cause overflow"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression has an @ attribute that is not recognized. Valid attributes are @jump_table. Check the spelling of the attribute name."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0270",
              "id": "P0270",
              "name": "Unknown match attribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@<name> not recognized in match attributes"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression has a malformed @ attribute. The attribute name must be a valid identifier (e.g., @jump_table)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0271",
              "id": "P0271",
              "name": "Malformed match attribute",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match attribute syntax error"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression was marked with @jump_table but the coverage is too sparse (less than 50% density or range > 256). The elaborator will emit a cmp/je fallback chain instead of a dense jump table. To enable jump-table dispatch, ensure at least 50% coverage of the range and arm count <= 256."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0272",
              "id": "P0272",
              "name": "@jump_table density too sparse",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match is too sparse for jump-table codegen; reverting to cmp/je chain"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: This match has @jump_table set, but the full codegen (rodata synthesis + memory-indirect jmp) is deferred to issue pa-r15-009b. For now, the elaborator emits a cmp/je fallback chain. The jump-table dispatch will be implemented in a future release."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0273",
              "id": "P0273",
              "name": "@jump_table codegen deferred",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@jump_table codegen deferred to follow-up issue; using cmp/je fallback for now"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression marked with @jump_table lacks a default (_) arm. Jump-table dispatch requires an exhaustive default case for bounds-checking the dispatch index. Add a default arm with `_ => <expr>`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0274",
              "id": "P0274",
              "name": "@jump_table requires default arm",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match with @jump_table must have a default arm (_)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #964: A match expression marked with @jump_table has a non-integer-literal arm (e.g., a variable or string pattern). Jump-table dispatch requires all arms (except the default _) to be integer literals so the elaborator can compute density and generate the dispatch offset. Convert non-literal patterns to integer literals or remove @jump_table."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0275",
              "id": "P0275",
              "name": "@jump_table requires integer-literal arms",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "match with @jump_table must have integer-literal patterns only"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1041: the current System-V x86-64 lowering passes lambda parameters in RDI, RSI, RDX, RCX, R8, R9. Stack-spill of the 7th+ parameter is not yet implemented. Reduce the parameter count to 6 or fewer, or split the function into curried groups (each group is a separate lambda)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0276",
              "id": "P0276",
              "name": "Lambda has more than 6 parameters",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "lambda arity exceeds System-V register-passed cap (6)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1071 (pa-r17-010b): A struct field declaration is syntactically incomplete. Ensure all fields follow the pattern `name: type`, separated by commas, with proper opening and closing braces. Trailing commas are allowed. Example: `struct S { x: u64, y: u32 }`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0277",
              "id": "P0277",
              "name": "Malformed struct field declaration",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "expected field name, colon, type, or closing brace"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1012: A @guid compile-time directive has an invalid GUID string. GUID syntax is XXXXXXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXX-XXXXXXXXXXXX (36 characters with dashes at positions 8, 13, 18, 23; all other characters must be hexadecimal). Verify the string is 36 characters, dashes are in the correct positions, and all hex characters are valid (0-9, a-f, A-F)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0278",
              "id": "P0278",
              "name": "Malformed GUID literal",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@guid literal malformed (wrong length, invalid dashes, non-hex characters)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1013: The @include_bytes compile-time directive encountered an error resolving or reading the file. Common causes: empty path, absolute path (only relative paths allowed), file not found, permission denied, or path is not a regular file. Verify the path is relative, the file exists, and the file is readable."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0279",
              "id": "P0279",
              "name": "@include_bytes path error",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@include_bytes path is invalid, not found, or inaccessible"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1013: The file referenced by @include_bytes is larger than the 16 MiB size limit for compile-time embeds. This limit is enforced to prevent accidentally embedding very large files during compilation. Split the data into smaller files or use a different approach (e.g., external file references) for larger payloads."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0280",
              "id": "P0280",
              "name": "@include_bytes file too large",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@include_bytes file exceeds 16 MiB limit"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Issue #1014: The @include_str directive requires the referenced file to be valid UTF-8. The file contains an invalid UTF-8 byte sequence at the indicated byte offset. Use @include_bytes_as_str instead if you need to embed binary data without UTF-8 validation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0281",
              "id": "P0281",
              "name": "@include_str file is not valid UTF-8",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@include_str: file is not valid UTF-8"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010: The @link_section directive's name must be a valid identifier containing only letters, digits, dots, underscores, and hyphens. The name must be 1–32 characters long and non-empty. Example: `let payload : [u8; 8] = ... @link_section(\".uefi_hdr\")`."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0282",
              "id": "P0282",
              "name": "Invalid @link_section name",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section name must match [A-Za-z0-9._-], length 1..32"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010: A let binding has multiple @link_section directives, which is not allowed. Remove all but one @link_section directive. Example: `let x = ... @link_section(\".foo\") @link_section(\".bar\")` is invalid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0283",
              "id": "P0283",
              "name": "Duplicate @link_section directive",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section appears more than once on the same binding"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-010 (MVP deferred to pa-r19-010b): The @link_section attribute is currently supported only on let bindings with data (literal, array) values. Lambda-shaped bindings (let x = fn(...)) are not yet supported. This is deferred to a future phase. Rewrite the binding without @link_section or defer the attribute."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0284",
              "id": "P0284",
              "name": "Lambda bindings cannot use @link_section",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@link_section not yet supported on lambda-shaped let bindings"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-001: The @abi directive must specify a valid calling convention string. Valid options are \"ms\" (Microsoft x64 ABI for UEFI) and \"sysv\" (System V AMD64 ABI). The string must be lowercase, enclosed in double quotes, and passed as the sole argument to @abi. Examples: `@abi(\"ms\")` or `@abi(\"sysv\")`. Invalid strings, non-string arguments, missing parentheses, or empty strings all trigger this error."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0285",
              "id": "P0285",
              "name": "Invalid @abi(...) value",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@abi requires \"ms\" or \"sysv\" (case-sensitive lowercase)"
              }
            },
            {
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Phase 19 PA19-r19-001: The @abi calling-convention directive is intended for function-shaped bindings (lambdas). You have applied @abi to a let binding with a non-function value (literal, array, etc.). Remove the @abi directive or rewrite the binding as a lambda. Example: `let f = fn(...) -> ... @abi(\"ms\")` is valid, but `let x : u64 = 42 @abi(\"ms\")` is invalid."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://paideia-os.org/diagnostics/P0286",
              "id": "P0286",
              "name": "@abi directive only valid on function-shaped bindings",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "@abi applied to non-lambda let binding"
              }
            },
